  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through nine innings, Walton broke it open with one swing in the tenth.",
    "what_this_means": "Late innings are where this team finds itself. Butler had driven in two and kept them close through six, but the game hung on a knife's edge until the moment it didn't. Walton's home run ended a night that could have gone either way, converting a roster full of working hitters. Fourteen hits total, only two runs from runners in scoring position. Into a win that mattered. The bullpen held through five innings of one-run baseball. Chris Roycroft closed it without drama. This is not a polished victory. This is the kind you take when you're still learning how to finish games.",
    "what_to_watch": "Bryan Woo has thrown four-plus innings of clean relief recently, and Seattle's lineup is swinging at everything with a .229 average. Jump gets a soft landing tonight at 6:40 PT, but one win does not erase the gulf between this team and a real contender.",
